<p>Pauline Hanson’s One Nation won the Farrer by-election in southern New South Wales on Saturday, giving the party its first elected seat in Australia’s House of Representatives after One Nation’s David Farley defeated independent Michelle Milthorpe. With more than 80% of ballots counted, Michael West Media reported Farley had more than 57% of the two-candidate-preferred vote. The seat had been held by the Liberal or National parties since 1949 and was previously represented by former opposition leader Sussan Ley. Hanson said One Nation was “coming after those other seats,” while party statements after the vote focused on lowering living costs, ending net-zero policies and stopping mass migration. The result does not affect Prime Minister Anthony Albanese’s parliamentary majority because Farrer had been held by the Liberal Party. Liberal shadow treasurer Tim Wilson said he wanted Liberal candidates to beat One Nation candidates, while Nationals MP Colin Boyce told The Guardian he was considering moving to One Nation after what he called a “wake-up call”.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/sTKL-LptHeRgqDaYDEgQQfM4qfu4zDYZ3_22MN6LD01k-3Ngei4xy6j5uGeDDixnw-_7uWGIuOsG22s_IKpYUMO1uISEthvJpfbyVg-p2g' alt='A campaign cutout depicting One Nation leader Pauline Hanson is displayed outside a pre-polling centre ahead of the Farrer by-election in Corowa, Australia.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Senate presence: One Nation already has four Senate seats, and Aaj News reported the party was polling second nationally this year, ahead of the Coalition.</li><li>Migration debate: About half of Australia’s 27 million people were either born overseas or have a parent who was.</li></ul><blockquote>We’re coming after those other seats - Pauline Hanson</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Pauline Hanson: Hanson posted on X that One Nation would fight in Parliament to lower living costs, end net-zero policies and stop mass migration. (<a href='https://english.aaj.tv/news/330458747/australias-populist-party-vows-to-fight-mass-migration-after-winning-first-lower-house-seat'>Aaj News</a>)</li><li>Angus Taylor: The Liberal leader said his party would take “hard lessons” from the Farrer result after the Coalition vote fell in the former Liberal stronghold. (<a href='https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/may/09/farrer-byelection-results-one-nation-michelle-milthorpe-coalition'>The Guardian</a>)</li><li>Colin Boyce: The Nationals MP for Flynn said he was considering a move to One Nation and said “everybody should be thinking about their political future” after the Farrer result. (<a href='https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/may/10/nationals-mp-colin-boyce-says-hes-considering-move-to-one-nation-after-wake-up-call-in-farrer-byelection'>The Guardian</a>)</li><li>Tim Wilson: The Liberal shadow treasurer did not rule out the Coalition forming a minority government with One Nation, but said he wanted Liberal candidates to beat One Nation candidates. (<a href='https://www.9news.com.au/national/farrer-byelection-2026-results-existential-crisis-liberal-party-coalition-one-nation/cfb453bc-599a-4991-88cc-3fe74f8a7749'>9News</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/may/10/pressure-mounts-on-angus-taylor-as-pauline-hanson-declares-one-nation-here-for-the-long-haul'>Pressure mounts on Angus Taylor as Pauline Hanson declares One Nation ‘here for the long haul’</a> - theguardian.com</li><li><a href='https://michaelwest.com.au/one-nation-eyes-more-seats-after-by-election-triumph/'>One Nation eyes more seats after by-election triumph</a> - michaelwest.com.au</li><li><a href='https://japantoday.com/category/world/australia%27s-trump-aligned-populists-vow-to-fight-mass-migration-after-winning-first-lower-house-seat'>Australia&#x27;s right-wing One Nation party vows to fight mass migration after winning first lower house seat</a> - japantoday.com</li><li><a href='https://www.abc.net.au